{
  "format": "sh-texture-upscale",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Textures with lettering for AI texture upscaling (texture_upscale): the network repaints small letters into other shapes, so these are scaled with a Lanczos filter instead and keep their text as the original draws it. \"name\" is the texture as <FOLDER>/<NAME> under convert/textures/ (it covers the palette variants <NAME>.<label> too); without \"rects\" the whole picture is filtered, with \"rects\" ([x, y, w, h] in texels of the imported picture) only those rectangles are, over the network's result. A mod adds entries with a file of the same path in its own folder (records merge by \"name\"; \"$remove\": true takes one out). A changed entry makes its picture again.",
